From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Stokes <git@tombl.dev>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:38:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add wasm32- and wasm64-unknown-linux-musl targets

Tier 3 targets for the tombl/linux NOMMU kernel port: musl libc, static
executables linked through the clang driver for the same triple, wasm
threads over an imported shared memory. They differ from
wasm32-wali-linux-musl in ABI (ordinary ILP32/LP64 C ABI, syscalls
through musl rather than host imports), which the "wali" vendor now
distinguishes.
