+# `wasm32-unknown-linux-musl` and `wasm64-unknown-linux-musl`
+
+**Tier: 3**
+
+WebAssembly executables for [tombl/linux](https://github.com/tombl/linux), a
+NOMMU Linux kernel port that runs in a WebAssembly host (a browser or Node.js)
+and runs each process as a wasm instance over a shared memory. Userspace is
+musl libc; programs enter the kernel through musl's ordinary syscall path
+rather than importing syscalls from the host as
+[WALI](wasm32-wali-linux.md) does.
+
+`wasm32-unknown-linux-musl` is ILP32 (`c_long` is 32 bits). `wasm64` uses
+memory64 and is LP64.
+
+## Target maintainers
+
+None upstream; maintained in the [tombl/rust](https://github.com/tombl/rust)
+fork.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Executables only, always statically linked; there is no dynamic loader.
+- `panic=abort`; wasm cannot unwind.
+- The `atomics` and `bulk-memory` features are enabled, since threads are
+  wasm threads over the shared process memory.
+- `std` is supported, apart from `fork` (the kernel is NOMMU; use
+  `posix_spawn`/`vfork`-style process creation) and `mmap` of files.
+
+## Building the target
+
+Linking goes through a clang for the same triple with a musl sysroot, from
+the tombl/llvm-project fork. The standard library is not shipped; build it
+with `-Zbuild-std` or `x.py` with a C toolchain for the target configured.
+
+## Building Rust programs
+
+```sh
+cargo +nightly build -Zbuild-std=std,panic_abort --target wasm32-unknown-linux-musl
+```
+
+## Testing
+
+There is no test runner in this repository; the
+[distro](https://github.com/tombl/distro) runs smoke tests in the kernel.
